{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116137,"nonce":"qhMOjxTJn/5dzYws9/zbJfzTU28=","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nThe spike resolved this spec's `rwa watch` mechanism empirically. Scope and\nAcceptance stand.\n\n**`rwa watch` is one file write. No game-side code at all.** `run-agent.sh`\nlaunches under mangohud with `MANGOHUD_CONFIGFILE` pointed at\n`_RimWorld-Agent/config/mangohud-agent.conf`. MangoHud watches that file, so\nrewriting its `fps_limit` line re-caps a RUNNING game within a second or two.\nDemonstrated live mid-measurement (free-run ~34 fps snapped to a locked 30.0,\nno restart). Default unwatched 30; raise to 60 only for live interactive\nwatching. Do not raise fps for `advance` — a 30 fps cap costs the budgeted\ntick loop nothing (FINDINGS section 6).\n\n**Revealing the window is separate from raising the cap, and the window is\nalready parked.** `run-agent.sh` applies\n`hyprctl keyword windowrule \"workspace special:rwagent silent, match:class ^(RimWorldLinux)$\"`\nbefore launch. `silent` is what keeps focus from moving. Verified by the\norchestrator: window on `special:rwagent`, active window unchanged. So `rwa\nwatch on` = reveal that workspace + write fps_limit=60; `off` = hide + write 30.\n\n**Do not assume a bare launch is a live game.** Hyprland delivers no frames to a\nhidden special workspace and RimWorld's tick loop is frame-bound, so an\nunpatched parked bench runs at 1-2 fps ~= 4 tps and looks perfectly healthy in\n`ps`. `run-agent.sh` already applies the three-part fix (render_unfocused,\nmisc:render_unfocused_fps, vblank_mode=0) — but for this spec's \"game not\nrunning\" detection: distinguish *no heartbeat* (game down) from *heartbeat with\na flat tick counter* (game frame-starved or genuinely paused). Both deserve\ndistinct, actionable messages; only the first should say \"how to start it\".\n\n**Bench path override.** `make-profile-agent.sh` honors `RIMWORLD_VAULT`\n(default `/home/dorian/projects/rimworld`), so the RIMWORLD_VAULT pattern this\nspec asks for is already the profile's own convention — reuse the same env var\nrather than inventing a second one.\n\n**Xvfb is a genuine fallback, not the daily driver.** With the render-unfocused\nfix proven on the live session, `--xvfb [--vnc]` exists in `run-agent.sh` for\nfully detached runs (lock screen, headless boot). Its runtime demo is still\nUNVERIFIED-PENDING-INSTALL of `xorg-server-xvfb`/`x11vnc` (FINDINGS section 8).\n\n**batchmode writes no Player.log** — Unity logs to stdout in that mode. If\nanything here ever scrapes logs, it must read the launcher's captured stdout.\nbatchmode is not the v1 path regardless (23 texture-atlas NREs).","files":null}]}